Well, that only took about 3 years :P

This was about my fourth time down to Gehennom, and the second time
that I've reached the Sanctum. As I recall, I accidentally stoned
myself with a cockatrice corpse the last time I got to Moloch's
sanctum. How sad is that?

Anyway, this is a pretty standard YAFAP post, right down to being a
Valkyrie, so I won't bore you with all the gory details (which I don't
really remember anyway). Suffice to say that I was amazed at how
smoothly this game went. I had all the desireable intrinsics except for
teleport control (I finally broke down and just wished for a ring
thereof - never did find one apart from that). I also had my ideal
armor profile, and only had to wish for a cloak of displacement to
complete it. The rest I found before the castle, except for the helm of
brilliance, which showed up randomly in Gehennom.

I ascended at XL30 with 484 HP, -35 AC, and around 150 energy. This
turned out to probably be overkill. The planes were far less harrowing
than I was expecting. I had one run-in with an archon, but I was
victorious with about 400 HP left. I had 3 AoLS, but never had to use
any of them. I think the only major mistake I made in the game was
accidentally eating a captain corpse. But since I had stealth, even
that wasn't really major. I've learned from this ascension that:

1) Rings of conflict are both awesome and hillarious.
They make speed running through the planes much easier, and greatly
mitigate the threat of summoning monsters like archons, Rodney, liches,
etc. I got double-teamed by two Rodneys and the high priest of Moloch
in the sanctum, all of whom were trying to summon creatures left and
right. It was really the only major challenge I encountered. But there
were two black dragons, a cockatrice, and a purple worm trapped in the
room with them. I just sat back and tried not to die laughing while
trying to see who would stone, eat, or disintigrate whom, first.

2) Bravely running away is underrated.
Seriously, the planes are much, much easier if you have a crap-load of
wands of  teleport with you. Odin's altar was the last one I checked,
but I was able to zip through them all in just a few minutes. If you
speed run through the planes, there's not much that can wrong. For the
most part, you can just flat out ignore the riders by cutting a path
around them. I think I could have cleared out the astral plane, in
retrospect, but since this was shaping up to be my first ascension, I
didn't want to risk it. Running is also very good when you find that
the entire left half of Medusa's level has been overrun with by a
mongolian horde of gremlins and a summoning titan.

Hmmm...what to play next? Wizards seem to be a popular choice, but I
can't quite decide.



